but he then came into his own lair,
and upon both of them sent an unseemly doom;
so will Odysseus send an unseemly doom upon those men.

There comes here regularly a certain one, the unerring old man of the sea,
immortal Proteus the Egyptian, who of the sea
entire the depths knows, a servant of Poseidon;

When early-born appeared, rose-fingered Dawn,
and then indeed along the shore of the wide-wayed sea
I went, greatly entreating the gods;
